---
name: autonomous_authorization_patterns
version: 2
priority: 100
condition: ~
patterns:
  - fully autonomous
  - hands-off
  - hands off
  - don't ask me
  - don't ask us
  - do not ask me
  - do not ask us
  - without asking me
  - without asking us
  - unattended
  - keep going until done without checking
  - you decide everything
  - just do it all
  - no check-ins
  - work autonomously
  - work in the background
  - run in the background
  - 别问我
  - 不用问我
  - 不要问我
  - 无需确认
  - 不用确认
  - 不要确认
  - 别确认
  - 自己决定
  - 你自己决定
  - 你看着办
  - 你自己办
  - 一口气做完
  - 一次做完
  - 一次做完它
  - 全部做完
  - 直接做完
  - 自己跑完
  - 跑完它
  - 独立完成
  - 不用管我
  - 不要中断
  - 别打断
  - 中途不用汇报
  - 不用汇报进度
---

Phrase patterns that signal explicit user authorization for hands-off,
long-chain autonomous execution. When the user's instruction matches any of
these, the checkpoint gate is disabled for the run: the user asked the agent
to work unattended, so pausing mid-chain would fight their explicit intent.

Matching is case-insensitive and substring-based, and is applied to the
current user message plus the most recent user turns (see
`checkpoint_gate_relaxed` and `recent_user_texts` in `encre.loop_stability`),
so an authorisation given once -- "你自己跑完，我要出门了" -- keeps covering the
task it was given for. The list stays deliberately specific so ordinary
instructions do not accidentally disable the gate.
